class Solution {
    public int arrangeCoins(int n) {
        // 'row' keeps track of how many complete rows we can form
        int row = 0;

        // Continue forming rows as long as we have enough coins
        // for the next row (which needs row + 1 coins)
        while (n >= row + 1) {
            
            // Move to the next row
            row++;
            
            // Subtract the number of coins used to fill this row
            n -= row;
        }

        // Return the total number of complete rows formed
        return row;
    }
}
Quick idea:
Row 1 needs 1 coin, row 2 needs 2 coins, row 3 needs 3 coins, etc.
Keep subtracting until you can’t build the next row.
The number of successful rows is your answer.
